WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.940
Put a pea plant in sterilised sand, and water it with a solution that holds no

2
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.460
nitrogen. Add a little soil extract.

3
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.260
The pea ends up with many times more nitrogen than its seed held.

4
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.580
An oat plant in the next pot starves.

5
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.020
Nitrogen gas makes up most of the air around both plants.

6
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.220
So why can one use it and the other not?

7
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:33.993
Hermann Hellriegel and Hermann Wilfarth tested this in pots, at an experiment

8
00:00:33.993 --> 00:00:35.413
station in Bernburg.

9
00:00:36.073 --> 00:00:37.813
They published in 1888.

10
00:00:38.973 --> 00:00:42.833
The solution held every mineral element but no nitrogen.

11
00:00:43.773 --> 00:00:47.533
The oats grew only as far as the nitrate they were given allowed.

12
00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:56.817
Now the peas. With no extract, they formed no nodules, and gained no nitrogen.

13
00:00:57.917 --> 00:01:03.297
Given a little extract of field soil, they formed nodules, which are swellings on

14
00:01:03.297 --> 00:01:07.237
the roots. These peas gained much nitrogen from the air.

15
00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:12.577
Extract that had been heated first gave no nodules and no gain.

16
00:01:13.537 --> 00:01:17.757
A living agent from soil, tied to the nodules, was required.

17
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.420
The experiment did not name that agent.

18
00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:27.660
In the same year, Martinus Beijerinck reported isolating bacteria from nodules.

19
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.800
They are called rhizobia.

20
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.720
They enter the root.

21
00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.620
Inside nodule cells they become bacteroids.

22
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.580
A bacteroid holds an enzyme called nitrogenase.

23
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.420
Nitrogenase reduces nitrogen gas to ammonia.

24
00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.780
The root itself makes no nitrogenase.

25
00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.470
In return, the plant supplies carbon.

26
00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:56.790
Sucrose from the leaves is converted to malate, and malate fuels the bacteroids.

27
00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:02.170
Oxygen damages nitrogenase, yet the bacteroids respire.

28
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:09.150
A plant protein called leghemoglobin binds oxygen and holds it at a low, steady

29
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.830
level. It does not keep oxygen out.

30
00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:18.290
In Lotus japonicus, silencing it raised free oxygen in nodules, and fixation

31
00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:23.190
stopped. The plants grew normally only when given mineral nitrogen.

32
00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:26.933
Oats and barley have no nodules.

33
00:02:27.733 --> 00:02:30.533
They depend on nitrate and ammonium in the soil.

34
00:02:31.573 --> 00:02:35.353
In those pots, oats had only the nitrate their solution held.

35
00:02:36.353 --> 00:02:38.373
A plant cannot make an element.

36
00:02:38.973 --> 00:02:42.513
It must take each one in, alone or with a partner.
